  "=== hearing",
  "present: ellis, june, jury, calloway, clearview",
  "~ remember world: ellis, danger, market (seen by jury, june) (strength 3)",
  "",
  "The prosecutor, Hal Calloway, is a pleasant man with a rugby player's neck and he does not waste the jury's time. He plays the scan on a screen the size of a wall: the 41 bus, from the driver's seat, rising onto the pavement, the market stalls going under. It lasts four seconds. Two jurors gasp. Juror four closes her eyes.",
  "",
  "Ellis watches the screen, not the jury. He's seen it a thousand times. He's never seen it from outside.",
  "",
  "* Object: the scan is trimmed. Demand the full recording",
  "  ~ remember truth, consent, full_record (seen by jury, calloway)",
  "      \"demanded the court see the whole recording\"",
  "  -> full_record",
  "* Ask for a recess, and get Ellis out of the room",
  "  ~ remember protect, comfort, ellis (seen by jury, ellis)",
  "      \"got your client out of the room before he had to watch it again\"",
  "  -> cross",
  "* Ask the court's permission to scan yourself, here, in front of the jury",
  "  ~ remember truth, consent, vulnerable",
  "      \"let the jury scan your own mind to show them what an unchosen thought looks like\"",
  "  ~ remember world: ellis, doubt (seen by jury) (strength 1.5)",
  "  -> own_scan",
  "",
  "",
  "=== own_scan",
  "The judge allows it, mostly out of curiosity. Calloway shrugs: rope, hanging. You hold the Lens to your own temple and the screen fills with what is in your head. Ellis's face. A wall. Your own car on the motorway, drifting, deliberately, toward the barrier. You have never told anyone that one either.",
  "",
  "The courtroom is very quiet. 'I've never done it,' you say. 'I never will. I don't know why it comes. Nobody does. That is the point.'",
  "",
  "* Turn off the screen and call the witness -> cross",
  "",
