  "=== cross",
  "present: ellis, june, jury, calloway, ravi, clearview",
  "",
  "{first visit: Ravi Sallis is thin and very polite, and he calls the judge 'sir' twice in the first minute. He says he saw a frightening image and did his civic duty. The judge has already told both counsel, twice, that she expects them to be brief.}",
  "{first visit and jury knows protect, ellis: When Ellis comes back in, two of the jurors watch him all the way to his seat. They saw you take him out before the screen went dark, and now they look at him as a man who needed taking out. # the jury saw the recess}",
  "{first visit and ravi_scanned == true: The Lens in your pocket weighs about as much as a stone. You know what he's afraid of. You could open him up like a tin.}",
  "{asked == \"when\": 'That afternoon,' Ravi says. 'I sat in a café for hours, sir. It isn't a small thing, to report a man. I wanted to be sure.'}",
  "{asked == \"count\": 'Sixty-one,' Ravi says, so quietly that the judge asks him to repeat it. He does. Somebody in the gallery laughs, once, without any humour in it.}",
  "{asked == \"shame\": Ravi opens his mouth and closes it again. 'Everybody has,' he says at last. 'Sir.' Juror four looks at him properly for the first time.}",
  "{asked == \"cafe\": 'The one by the market,' Ravi says, puzzled. 'With the green awning.' Calloway smiles into his notes. The jury has learned that the café has a green awning.}",
  "{visited cross >= 3: The judge leans forward. 'Last question, counsel. Make it count.'}",
  "",
