  "- not first visit:",
  "{prep == \"calloway\": You do Calloway's voice, flat and pleasant. 'How often does the image come, Mr Varga?' Ellis opens his mouth, closes it. 'Every day,' he says at last, to the table. Then, to you: 'That's the wrong answer, isn't it.' It isn't wrong. It's just the one that will be hardest to hear.}",
  "{prep == \"coat\": He has never said the man's name out loud. He says it now: Arturo. Arturo had a red coat and a bag of oranges and was crossing to the bus stop. Ellis was nine, holding his mother's hand on the opposite kerb. 'I don't see the crash,' he says. 'I see the moment just before. When it could still go either way.'}",
  "{prep == \"logs\": You lay the Clearview printouts in a row. Six scans in eight weeks, six strangers, the same red coat every time. Ellis reads them slowly. 'They all saw it,' he says. 'Six people on my bus saw the worst thing in my head, and not one of them said anything to me.'}",
  "",
  "{visited preparation >= 3: A guard knocks on the glass and holds up five fingers. Ellis rubs his eyes. 'Tell me what to do tomorrow,' he says. | The coffee has gone cold. Ellis waits to see what you'll ask him next.}",
  "- else:",
  "The night before Ellis testifies, you sit with him in a meeting room that smells of instant coffee. He wants to take the stand. He wants to say it himself. The risk is that Calloway will ask how often the image comes, and the true answer is every single day.",
  "{ellis knows expose, june: Before you can begin, he says: 'June told me you told her.' He doesn't say anything else for a while. When he does, it's: 'Let's just get on with it.'}",
  "{ellis knows lie, june: 'June thinks it's fake,' he says. 'She says you told her. I don't know how to tell her it isn't.'}",
  "}",
