  "=== testimony",
  "{",
  "- testimony == \"coached\":",
  "Ellis says it comes rarely. Only on bad days. Calloway nods sympathetically, then plays a Clearview log: six scans of Ellis in eight weeks, from six different commuters, each with the same image. 'Rarely, Mr Varga?' Ellis looks at you. Every juror sees him look at you.",
  "- testimony == \"silent\":",
  "Ellis does not testify. He sits beside you through the rest of the prosecution case with his hands folded, and the jury watches him the way you'd watch a dog that's never bitten anyone yet.",
  "- else:",
  "Ellis tells them all of it. The lorry in the market when he was nine. A man under the wheels in a red coat. The picture that comes every day since, at the same corner. 'And then I check the mirror,' he says. 'Nineteen years. Every time. I'm the most careful driver on that route because I can't stop seeing what happens if I'm not.' Juror four is crying, very quietly.",
  "}",
