  "=== gallery",
  "present: ellis, june",
  "",
  "In the corridor June is waiting for her father. She has been in the gallery every day.",
  "{june knows lie, june: She walks straight past him to you. 'You said it was fake,' she says. 'You said they made it up.' She has heard enough in that courtroom now to know it wasn't, and she is fifteen, and she does not know who to be angriest with. | She goes to him. She doesn't say anything. She puts her forehead on his chest the way she did when she was small, and Ellis puts one hand on the back of her head, and the court officer looks away.}",
  "",
