  "=== closing",
  "present: ellis, jury, calloway, ravi, clearview",
  "",
  "Closing arguments. The jury has seen four seconds of a bus mounting a pavement, and everything you've managed to put beside it. Calloway's closing is short and terrible: 'You saw what was in his head. Ask yourselves whether you'd put your children on that bus.'",
  "{calloway knows bounty: He doesn't mention Ravi Sallis once. Four hundred dollars a flag is not a number he wants back in their heads. # Calloway heard the price}",
  "{jury knows vulnerable: Juror four isn't watching Calloway. She is watching you, the way she has since you held the Lens to your own temple. # the jury saw your scan}",
  "",
  "* Ask them to judge what Ellis did, nineteen years of it, not what he saw",
  "  ~ remember truth, consent, closing (seen by jury, ellis)",
  "      \"asked the jury to judge him by what he did\"",
  "  ~ remember world: ellis, doubt (seen by jury)",
