  "=== verdict",
  "{",
  "- misconduct:",
  "The judge clears the jury. In chambers, Calloway is almost gentle about it: unauthorised scanning of a witness or juror by counsel is a crime, and everything after it is poisoned. Mistrial. Ellis will be tried again, with a new lawyer, before a new jury who will see the four seconds fresh. You are referred to the bar. Ellis watches them take your name down. He doesn't say anything at all.",
  "- juryTrustsEllis:",
  "The jury is out for five hours. When they come back the foreperson, a retired electrician, reads 'not guilty' without looking at the paper. Ellis doesn't move. You have to touch his arm to tell him he's allowed to stand up.",
  "- else:",
  "The jury is out for two days. When they come back, none of them look at Ellis. Guilty of conspiracy to commit a vehicular attack. Ellis nods as if this is something he has been expecting since he was nine. In the gallery June makes a sound you will hear for the rest of your career.",
  "}",
